Hi all,

A short summary of the outcome from today’s discussion with the Backup
Team regarding the Storage Protect setup on p3lah002.

The main decisions are:

-   We have the green light to proceed with the installation of IBM
    Storage Protect Server 8.1.25 on p3lah002.
-   LA HUB will install four local Storage Protect server instances on
    the AIX host as planned.
-   This allows us to proceed with the APAC extract/insert migration as
    the first migration step.
-   The existing Backup Team setup on p3lah002 remains unchanged as part
    of this migration:
    -   SP Client 8.1.25
    -   Storage Agent 8.1.25
    -   Backup Team Storage Protect infrastructure

For the future Storage Protect lifecycle upgrade, we agreed on a phased
approach:

-   Backup Team can upgrade its own Storage Protect infrastructure
    independently.
-   The local Storage Agent on p3lah002 will be upgraded separately
    together with the local LA HUB Storage Protect Server installation.
-   During any interim period where the local STA is not aligned with
    the Backup Team SP server level, LAN-free backup through STA will
    not be used.
-   Required backups will continue via the SP Client over LAN until the
    local STA and SP Server upgrade is completed.

The immediate next step for LA HUB is therefore to proceed with the SP
Server 8.1.25 installation on p3lah002 and continue preparation for the
APAC migration.

Thanks to the Backup Team for the support and alignment.

